## 9. Understanding the Reverse Method

The reverse method uses two pointers.

```java
private static void reverse(int[] nums, int left, int right) {

    while (left < right) {

        int temp = nums[left];

        nums[left] = nums[right];

        nums[right] = temp;

        left++;
        right--;
    }
}
```

### How It Works

For example:

```text
[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
```

Initial pointers:

```text
left = 0
right = 4
```

Swap:

```text
[5, 2, 3, 4, 1]
```

Move both pointers inward.

Swap:

```text
[5, 4, 3, 2, 1]
```

The pointers meet, so the reversal is complete.

This is a common two-pointer pattern used in many array and string problems.

