## 12. Complexity Analysis

Let `n` be the length of the array.

| Approach | Time Complexity | Extra Space |
|---|---|---|
| Brute Force | O(n × k) | O(1) |
| Extra Array | O(n) | O(n) |
| Reversal Algorithm | O(n) | O(1) |

### Why Is Reversal O(n)?

We perform three reversals:

1. Reverse the entire array: O(n).
2. Reverse the first k elements: O(k).
3. Reverse the remaining elements: O(n - k).

Total:

```text
O(n) + O(k) + O(n - k)

= O(3n)

= O(n)
```

We use only a temporary variable and two pointers, so extra space is O(1).

